IMPORT prelude

-- Legal Profession Uniform Law (Victoria) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the
-- daydate library. The Law counts in days ("within 30 days after", s 187(2); "within 21 days after", s 187(3); "at least
-- 30 days after", s 194(2)(b); "30 days or more after", s 195(2); "60 days after", s 272(3)), in months ("within 12
-- months after", s 198(3); "more than 6 months after", s 195(5); "within 4 months after", s 272(2)(a)) and in clear
-- business days ("not less than 5 clear business days", s 181(4)). The Victorian Act s 99(2) counts "within 60 days after".
--
-- A period of months after a day ends on the same day of the month that many months later; where that month has no such
-- day, on its last day (fork F1). A business day is a day that is not a Saturday, Sunday or a public, special or bank
-- holiday in the place (s 6); the holidays are given as a list of dates.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Legal
-- Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2014 (Vic), Version No. 018 (11 October 2023), whose Schedule 1 is the Legal
-- Profession Uniform Law, not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the authority of the
-- Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with the Copyright Act
-- 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Legal Profession Uniform Law (Victoria)`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `the first` `is before` `the second` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `the first` `is on or before` `the second` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second`

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first` `and` `the second` MEANS
    IF `the day` `the first` `is before` `the second`
    THEN `the second`
    ELSE `the first`

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` `the first` `and` `the second` MEANS
    IF `the day` `the first` `is before` `the second`
    THEN `the first`
    ELSE `the second`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` y IF
        (y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0)
    AND (    (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
         OR  (y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0))

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    BRANCH IF m EQUALS 2 THEN IF `is a leap year` y THEN 29 ELSE 28
           IF m EQUALS 4 THEN 30
           IF m EQUALS 6 THEN 30
           IF m EQUALS 9 THEN 30
           IF m EQUALS 11 THEN 30
           OTHERWISE 31

-- The same day of the month, n calendar months later (the last day of that month where it has no such day).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the same day` n `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the day of the month` `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `months counted from January` MEANS (DATE_MONTH `the start` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the new year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS FLOOR (`months counted from January` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the new month` MEANS (`months counted from January` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the day of the month` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the start` GREATER THAN `the number of days in month` `the new month` `of` `the new year`
            THEN `the number of days in month` `the new month` `of` `the new year`
            ELSE DATE_DAY `the start`

-- The day of the week: 0 is Sunday, 6 is Saturday (DATE_SERIAL counts so that 6 July 2026, a Monday, gives 1).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekday of` `the day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a business day` `the day` `given the holidays` `the holidays` IF
        (NOT (`the weekday of` `the day` EQUALS 0))
    AND (NOT (`the weekday of` `the day` EQUALS 6))
    AND (NOT (any (GIVEN h YIELD DATE_SERIAL h EQUALS DATE_SERIAL `the day`) `the holidays`))

-- The n-th business day after a day (the day itself not counted: "clear" days, fork F2). n is at least 1.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE, `the holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the business day` n `after` `the start` `given the holidays` `the holidays` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN `the start`
    ELSE IF `is a business day` `the next day` `given the holidays` `the holidays`
         THEN `the business day` (n MINUS 1) `after` `the next day` `given the holidays` `the holidays`
         ELSE `the business day` n `after` `the next day` `given the holidays` `the holidays`
    WHERE
        `the next day` MEANS `the date` 1 `days after` `the start`
